.\" onis(1): Oniscus welcome screen and system Swiss army knife
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH ONIS 1 "October 2026" "Oniscus" "Oniscus Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
onis, oniscus \- Oniscus welcome screen and system Swiss army knife
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onis
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B onis help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B onis
.I command
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B onis
is the Oniscus control center for the terminal. With no command it opens the
welcome screen, a keyboard menu that installs and removes apps, updates the
system, manages snapshots, changes the accent color and i3 shortcuts, and opens
an AI agent that knows the system. Every menu item is also a subcommand, so the
same actions work in scripts.
.PP
The menu opens by itself at login, and from anywhere with
.BR Super+Alt+Space ,
where it is shown in
.BR rofi (1).
Actions that need a terminal open in a floating one.
.PP
Commands that change the system run
.BR sudo (8)
and print the exact command before running it.
.B oniscus
is an alternative name for
.BR onis .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Apps
.TP
.BR install " [\fIapp\fR]"
With no argument, opens the install tab: "Install another package" at the top,
then the categories AI agents, Browsers, Office, Design, Development,
Communication, Media, Games, Utilities and Drivers and codecs.
With
.IR app ,
installs it directly. The app may be a command (\fBclaude\fR), a package name,
a Flathub ID or a name from the catalog. If it is not in the catalog, the
Tumbleweed repositories and Flathub are searched.
.IP
Sources, in order of preference: the official Tumbleweed repositories
.RB ( zypper ),
Flathub
.RB ( "flatpak \-\-user" ,
no sudo; the remote is added per user on first use), and for AI agents the
project's official installer or npm into
.IR ~/.local .
.TP
.BR uninstall " [\fB\-\-purge\fR] [\fIapp\fR]"
With no argument, opens a menu to pick an AI agent, Flatpak app or system
package, then either remove the app only or remove and purge. Before removing a
system package it runs a zypper dry run, shows the list, and refuses if a
protected package (kernel, systemd, zypper, i3, XFCE, Ly, gum, flatpak and
others) would be removed.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-purge
Also remove orphaned dependencies
.RB ( "zypper remove \-\-clean\-deps" ),
Flatpak app data and unused runtimes
.RB ( "\-\-delete\-data" ", " "\-\-unused" ),
and offer to delete the app's folders in
.IR ~/.config ,
.I ~/.local/share
and
.IR ~/.cache .
.RE
.TP
.B uninstall \-\-cleanup
Remove packages nothing needs anymore
.RB ( "zypper packages \-\-unneeded" ),
run
.BR "zypper clean \-\-all" " and " "flatpak uninstall \-\-unused" ,
and prune old i3 config backups made by
.BR onis .
.TP
.BR drivers " [" nvidia | codecs ]
Optional extras that cannot ship in the ISO, using the same commands as the
installer's optional screens.
.B nvidia
installs the proprietary driver from NVIDIA's official openSUSE repository
(checks for an NVIDIA card with
.BR lspci (8)
first).
.B codecs
adds the third-party Packman repository and installs multimedia codecs, after a
patent warning.
.SS System
.TP
.BR update " [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Update system packages with
.B zypper refresh
and
.B zypper dup
(the correct way on Tumbleweed), then user and system Flatpak apps.
snapper takes restore points before and after; without its zypper plugin,
.B onis
takes one before. At the end it says whether a restart is needed.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-\-yes ", " \-y
Ask nothing; zypper runs non-interactively. Meant for scripts.
.RE
.TP
.BR snapshot " [" list | create | diff | delete | rollback ]
Manage system restore points made by
.BR snapper (8)
on the root filesystem.
.I /home
is a separate subvolume, so these never touch user files. With no argument,
opens a menu.
.RS
.TP
.B list
Show snapshots, newest first.
.B *
marks the running one,
.B +
the one used at the next boot.
.TP
.BR create " [\fIdescription\fR]"
Take a snapshot now.
.TP
.BR diff " \fIn\fR [\fIm\fR]"
List files changed between snapshot
.I n
and
.I m
(default: the running system).
.TP
.BR delete " \fIn\fR"
Delete snapshot
.IR n .
Refuses the running and the default snapshot.
.TP
.BR rollback " \fIn\fR"
Make the system boot as it was in snapshot
.I n
from the next restart
.RB ( "snapper rollback" ).
The current state is kept as a snapshot.
.RE
.TP
.B doctor
Print a read-only system report: failed services, journal errors, crashed
programs, disk, memory, network, sound, repositories, Flatpak apps, snapshots,
i3 config validation and
.B onis
state. The output is always in English so AI agents read it the same way.
.TP
.B restart-bars
Restart Polybar, xfce4-panel and Plank.
.TP
.B about
Show system information with
.BR fastfetch (1).
.SS AI agents
.TP
.BR agent " [\fBask\fR \fItask\fR]"
Open the default AI agent in its working folder
.IR ~/.local/share/oniscus/agent ,
which holds the Oniscus guide as
.IR AGENTS.md ,
.I CLAUDE.md
and
.IR GEMINI.md .
With no task, asks what to solve first. Shortcut:
.BR Super+Ctrl+Shift+a .
.TP
.BR "agent default" " [\fIcommand\fR]"
Pick the default agent:
.BR claude ", " codex ", " gemini ", " opencode " or " hermes .
Installs it first if needed.
.TP
.BR "agent crashes" " " on | off
Offer the agent through a desktop notification when a program crashes
(watches systemd-coredump messages in the user journal).
.TP
.B agent link
Link the guide and the Oniscus skill into
.IR ~/.claude/skills ,
.IR ~/.codex/skills ,
.IR ~/.agents/skills ,
.I ~/.config/opencode/skills
and
.IR ~/.hermes/skills .
Runs at every login.
.SS Look and shortcuts
.TP
.BR accent " [\fI#RRGGBB\fR|\fBdefault\fR]"
Change the accent color in the user's copies of the i3 config, Polybar,
fastfetch, the Starship prompt, the GTK and rofi themes and the terminal cursor. With no
argument, opens a picker with seven presets or any hex color. The Ly login
screen changes only if the user accepts (sudo).
.TP
.BR wallpaper " [\fB\-\-apply\fR]"
Pick an image from
.IR /usr/share/wallpapers ,
.I ~/Pictures
or
.IR ~/Imagens .
.B \-\-apply
sets the saved choice with
.BR feh (1);
i3 runs it at startup.
.TP
.BR keys " [" show | change | new | remove | restore ]
Manage i3 shortcuts in
.IR ~/.config/i3/config .
Every change keeps a backup, refuses a key combination already in use,
validates with
.B i3 \-C
and restores the backup if i3 rejects it. Write keys as
.BR Super+Shift+t .
.B restore
brings back the original Oniscus config.
.SS Session
.TP
.B menu
Show the menu in rofi.
.TP
.BR welcome " [" on | off | \-\-autostart ]
Open the welcome screen, or turn opening at login on or off.
.B \-\-autostart
is used by i3 at login.
.TP
.BR help " [\fIcommand\fR]"
Show the command list, or the help for one command. Also available as
.IB command " \-\-help" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANG
The menu text follows the session language:
.B pt_*
shows Brazilian Portuguese, anything else shows English. Commands, file names
and the agent guide are always in English.
.TP
.B ONISCUS_LANG
Overrides
.B LANG
for
.B onis
only (for example
.BR ONISCUS_LANG=en ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/oniscus/catalog.tsv
Install catalog, one app per line (format described in the file).
.TP
.I /usr/share/oniscus/agent/AGENTS.md
Guide for AI agents: config map, safety rules and recipes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oniscus/
User state: accent color, wallpaper, default agent, preferences and the
Starship prompt copy.
.TP
.I ~/.config/i3/config.oniscus\-*
Backups of the i3 config made by
.BR "onis keys" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when a command fails or is refused.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
onis install claude
onis uninstall \-\-purge com.spotify.Client
onis update \-\-yes
onis snapshot create "before the new driver"
onis snapshot rollback 42
onis accent '#7AA2F7'
onis agent ask "Wi\-Fi stopped working after the update"
.fi
